<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!-- Full profile: tuned for devices with ample RAM (3+ GB), like an NVIDIA Shield.
     The setup service copies this to the user profile and self-heals after updates.
     Takes effect after a Kodi restart (Kodi reads advancedsettings.xml at startup).

     Texture resolution caps (imageres, fanartres):
     Kodi caps decoded texture size, expressed as pixel height at a 16:9 area.
     Kodi 21 defaults are imageres 540 and fanartres 1080.
       imageres 720: higher than default, trades memory for sharper art on large
       screens and higher resolutions. Still safe on 3+ GB devices.
       fanartres 1080: Kodi default; fanart and hero backgrounds can now be enabled
       in the skin for a richer visual presentation.

     Redraws are limited to dirty regions to ease the GPU.

     Video cache: Kodi 21 Omega moved cache settings into the GUI and ignores
     <cache> blocks here. The setup service now sets them through JSON-RPC to
     100-150 MB (larger buffer for 3+ GB devices). -->
<advancedsettings>
    <imageres>720</imageres>
    <fanartres>1080</fanartres>
    <gui>
        <algorithmdirtyregions>3</algorithmdirtyregions>
        <nofliptimeout>0</nofliptimeout>
    </gui>
</advancedsettings>
